WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.001
-Good evening, I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.002
This is "Late Night."

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.003
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.004
And if you don't mind,

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.338
we're gonna get to the news.

00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:09.609
President Biden said yesterday
that he was surprised

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:12.178
by the news that
classified documents were found

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:15.814
in his old think tank office,
and added he wasn't sure

00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:17.249
what was in the files.

00:00:17.249 --> 00:00:21.387
Ah, yes, the ol' "grandpa
caught shoplifting" maneuver.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:22.522
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.522
[ As Biden ]
"Uh-oh, what's that?

00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:24.824
There's something in my pocket?

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.694
Oh, a Charleston Chew?"

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.895
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.964
How could that happen?"

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.899
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.200
[ Normal voice ]
After classified documents

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.202
were found in his old
think tank office,

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.537
President Biden said yesterday,

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.972
"People know I take
classified documents,

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:41.641
classified information
seriously."

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:45.945
He then added, "Even the aliens
at Area 51 know that. Damn it!"

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.581
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.883
House Speaker Kevin McCarthy
presided over

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:53.586
a closed-door meeting yesterday
of the Republican Conference,

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.522
but they eventually let him in.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:57.957
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.026
C-SPAN formally
requested yesterday

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.727
that House Speaker
Kevin McCarthy

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:03.596
allow the network's
independent cameras

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.832
to cover the Chamber,
though McCarthy says

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:08.935
they first have to weigh
an offer from TMZ.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.571
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.940
The Rules Package approved
by the House this week

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.010
included a measure that would
allow members to cut salaries

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.111
of individual Federal employees.

00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:21.114 line:0%
Said Biden, "What the hell?!"

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:24.717
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:25.718
How am I gonna afford

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.253
my Charleston Chews?!"

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.488
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:30.990
According
to Financial Disclosures,

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.292
Georgia Republican Senate
nominee Herschel Walker

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:36.295
has more than $5 million
left in his campaign account,

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:39.565
though, needless to say,
someone should probably

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:40.934
check the math.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.802
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.802 --> 00:01:45.738
The Golden Globe Awards
were held last night,

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:48.441
and former child star
Ke Huy Quan

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.943
won best supporting actor
for his role in "Everything --"

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:53.713
Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.481
"Everything Everywhere
All at Once."

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.283
I mean, what a comeback story.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.852
I honestly never thought
we would see

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:01.220
the Golden Globes again.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.657
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:07.293
According to a new survey,
the average teenager

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.328
is first exposed
to online pornography

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:12.665
by 12 years old,
despite the strict controls

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.133
in place to stop it.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:17.103
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.675
It seems foolproof.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.109
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:27.247
On this day in 1935,
pilot Amelia Earhart

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:29.081
made the first
successful solo flight

00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:32.051
from Hawaii to California,
and I think we can all agree

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.953
it made her
a little too confident.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:37.423
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:45.098
[ Laughter continues ]

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:47.766
And finally, a 9-year-old
in Maryland recently found

00:02:47.766 --> 00:02:50.603
a tooth of an extinct
megalodon shark,

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.538
and this is weird,
in a McNugget.

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.940
You guys...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.943
...that was a mo--
that was a monologue.

